  "answer": "Citation complaints declined sharply from Q1 to Q2. In Q1 2026, there was a sharp increase in tickets related to citation errors [NL-010#NL-010-S05], with monthly citation accuracy tickets at 72 (Jan), 79 (Feb), and 88 (Mar) [NL-011#NL-011-S05]. After the April fix was deployed, Q2 saw a steady decline to 42 (Apr), 31 (May), and 24 (Jun) [NL-011#NL-011-S05]. Citation-related complaints decreased significantly [NL-016#NL-016-S04], and user complaints regarding incorrect or missing citations dropped significantly [NL-011#NL-011-S03].\n\nThe remaining scanned-document problem is directly addressed by the planned **Advanced OCR Pipeline**. This planned product work involves integrating a standard OCR engine into the KnowledgeHub ingestion queue and designing an interface to show text extraction quality scores, with a target to launch an OCR pilot by August 2026 [NL-010#NL-010-S10]. The pipeline is actively being developed and scheduled for release in August 2026 to automatically extract text and layout structures from scanned files, enabling page-specific citations [NL-024#NL-024-S04].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
